# --- Database (required) ---
# PostgreSQL. Locally: run `docker compose up -d` (see docker-compose.yml)
# and use the value below unchanged — it's a local-only dev credential,
# not a secret. In production (Vercel + Prisma Postgres), Vercel sets
# DATABASE_URL automatically when you connect the database to your
# project — never invent or reuse the local value there.
#
# One connection string covers both runtime queries and schema migrations
# (`prisma migrate deploy`) — that's how Vercel's Prisma Postgres
# integration is designed to work, so no second DIRECT_URL is needed. If
# you switch to a different Postgres provider that puts a plain pooler
# (PgBouncer, Supabase, Neon) in front of the database — one that does
# NOT support schema changes through the pooled connection — add a
# `directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")` line back into the datasource block in
# prisma/schema.prisma and set DIRECT_URL to that provider's unpooled
# connection string.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/dziflip"

# --- Photo upload storage (required for the file-upload "+ Přidat" button) ---
# A serverless function's own filesystem is ephemeral — uploaded photos
# must live in real persistent object storage. This app uses Vercel Blob
# (https://vercel.com/docs/storage/vercel-blob). In Vercel: Project →
# Storage → Create Database → Blob, then connect it to this project —
# Vercel injects BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN automatically, you never type or
# invent the value yourself. Locally, run `vercel env pull` after creating
# the store, or leave it unset — uploads then fail with a clear "úložiště
# není připojeno" error instead of pretending to work.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --- Future integrations (not required for MVP, app works without them) ---
# When set, activates the direct FlatScan Data API integration
# (src/lib/sources/flatScan/) — real automatic Comparable Discovery,
# Listing Discovery, price history and locality/district context for
# Sreality/Bezrealitky/iDNES-sourced listings that FlatScan itself
# aggregates. This is the ONLY environment variable needed — the moment
# FLATSCAN_API_KEY is set, Provider Health switches FlatScan from
# PENDING_ACCESS to CONNECTED and every dependent feature (comparables,
# price history, locality panel) activates automatically. Never logged,
# never returned in any API response. See DEPLOY.md for details.
# FLATSCAN_API_KEY=
# Base URL override — only needed if FlatScan gives you a different
# endpoint (e.g. a dedicated/regional one). Defaults to
# https://flatscan.cz/api/v1 when unset.
# FLATSCAN_API_BASE_URL=

# When set, activates the WEB_SEARCH provider (src/lib/sources/searchProvider.ts)
# — real automatic Comparable Discovery + Listing Discovery instead of manual
# entry. Point it at a licensed search/real-estate-data API you have access
# to (a SERP-style API or a data aggregator's REST endpoint); the app never
# scrapes a portal directly or fabricates results. See DEPLOY.md for the
# exact JSON response shape it expects.
# SEARCH_API_KEY=
# SEARCH_API_URL=

# When set, enables AI photo analysis (room recognition, condition assessment).
# VISION_API_KEY=

# When set, activates the real Google Gemini image-to-image provider
# (src/lib/imageGen/gemini/) for AI-generated after-renovation room
# visualizations — an actual edit of the ORIGINAL listing photo, never a
# newly invented room. Server-side only: never expose this as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_GEN_API_KEY, never log it, never return it to the
# client or store it in the database.
# IMAGE_GEN_API_KEY=
# Optional override of the Gemini model id used for image editing.
# Default: gemini-2.5-flash-image (confirmed production-ready, non-preview,
# per Google's own Developer Blog). A newer preview model such as
# gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview ("Nano Banana 2") can be selected here
# without a code change.
# GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=

# When set, activates the generic PRODUCT_SEARCH provider
# (src/lib/products/genericSearchProvider.ts) — real product search/refresh
# for the shopping list instead of PENDING_ACCESS. Point it at a licensed
# product-data API/feed you have access to; the app never scrapes a
# specific Czech e-shop or fabricates a product/price/URL.
# PRODUCT_SEARCH_API_KEY=
# PRODUCT_SEARCH_API_URL=

# When both are set, enables real outbound e-mail for viewing-request
# messages (Contact automation). Without them, messages are always
# prepared/logged but never claimed as sent (status BLOCKED_NO_PROVIDER).
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_FROM=

# When set, enables an approved data source for a real estate portal (e.g.
# Sreality.cz) in Deal Radar. Until then that provider stays PENDING_ACCESS
# and is never scraped or bypassed.
# SREALITY_API_KEY=

# When all three are set, enables the REAL_SMS provider (src/lib/sms/realProvider.ts).
# Without them, SMS Hub always uses MOCK_SMS for demo data and safely fails
# (never fakes a send) for real contacts. Adjust the request shape in
# realProvider.ts to match whichever CZ SMS gateway you choose.
# SMS_API_URL=
# SMS_API_KEY=
# SMS_SENDER_ID=

# Optional shared-secret check for the inbound SMS webhook
# (/api/sms/webhook), sent by your SMS provider as an X-Webhook-Secret
# header. Leave unset during local testing.
# SMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
